  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given two arrays AAA and BBB of length NNN each.\n\nYou can do the following operation on the array BBB **exactly once**:\n\n\nChose two integers RRR (1≤R≤N)(1 \\le R \\le N)(1≤R≤N) and K(K≥0)K(K \\ge 0)K(K≥0) and apply KKK right-rotations to the subarray [1,R][1,R][1,R].\n\nApplying a right-rotation to the array C=[C1,C2,C3,…,CM]C = [C_1, C_2, C_3, \\ldots, C_M]C=[C1​,C2​,C3​,…,CM​] changes it to [CM,C1,C2,…,C(M−1)][C_M, C_1, C_2, \\ldots, C_{(M-1)}][CM​,C1​,C2​,…,C(M−1)​]\nFind whether you can transform the array BBB into the array AAA by applying the mentioned operation **exactly** once. If it is possible, find the **minimum** value of KKK for which it is possible.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input contains an integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. TTT test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains the integer NNN - the size of arrays AAA and BBB.\nThe second line contains NNN integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ - the elements of the array AAA.\nThe third line contains NNN integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​ - the elements of the array BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output in a single line, the **minimum** possible value of KKK. If it is not possible to convert BBB to AAA, print `-1`.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\le T \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai,Bi≤1091 \\le A_i, B_i\\le 10^91≤Ai​,Bi​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN across all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4\n1 4 5 2\n4 5 1 2\n6\n1 2 3 4 5 6\n1 2 5 6 3 4",
        "output": "1\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Let R=3R = 3R=3 and K=1K = 1K=1. Thus, we apply 111 right-rotation on the subarray [4,5,1][4, 5, 1][4,5,1]. The rotated subarray is [1,4,5][1, 4, 5][1,4,5]. The updated array is [1,4,5,2][1, 4, 5, 2][1,4,5,2] which is equal to the array AAA.\nIt can be shown that the array BBB cannot be converted into the array AAA using KKK less than 111.\nTest case 222: The array BBB cannot be converted to the array AAA using the mentioned operation exactly once."
      }
    ]
  },
